# WinTAK 5.6 plugin — component-level ignores.
#
# This file and WinTAK5.7/.gitignore were byte-identical (273 b each) and duplicated the
# root .gitignore's .NET section (audit Appendix E §2.4). Collapsed to genuine deltas:
# bin/, obj/, packages/, .vs/, *.user, IDE and OS junk are all covered once at the
# repository root and must not be restated here.

# ── Genuine component delta: the vendored WinTAK SDK assemblies ──────────────
# `libs/` holds WinTAK SDK DLLs (TAK.Engine.dll and friends) copied from a local WinTAK
# install. They are correctly UNTRACKED — `git ls-files "*.dll"` returns 0 — but note that
# their redistribution terms are undocumented, and whether the built .wpk may legally embed
# them is an open licensing question. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md ("Unresolved") and
# QUESTIONS-FOR-OWNER.md. Populate from your local WinTAK install; see README.md.
libs/

# ── .wpk build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# build-wpk.py writes the plugin package here. The packaged artefact is a release output,
# not source; CI produces it and attaches a SHA-256 checksum (C-18, C-35).
*.wpk
dist/

# .NET test build output
Tests/**/bin/
Tests/**/obj/
